Z||000000||Cliff Pennock||09-30-2000||01:39 PM||||There was this two page editorial about the Fiero in one of our dutch car magazines. It was actually about a kit-car based on the Fiero. Here's one of the quotes from that magazine: "In the States the original Fiero's nickname is <I>f--king Fiero</I>, because of its bad handling."<P>I think by now it's safe to say that if you have no clue whatsoever about cars, if your IQ is about the same as your shoe-size, and if everytime you open your mouth they have to call a manure-truck, then you are eligible to become a writer for a car magazine.||||reg||8
